From: Marionette AirDrop driver research
Subject: [fuxi runtime] virtually allocate only the host PDEV preallocation context

0023 could not reach ordinary Wi-Fi or monitor creation: the captured stack
fails dp_prealloc_init+0x7c, table index 0, allocating 84592 bytes (order:5)
with ~577MiB total free but no order-5 pages. That entry is DP_PDEV_TYPE,
not a DMA ring and not the SoC context. Use existing zeroed qdf_mem_valloc
only for that context and pair qdf_mem_vfree in its owning prealloc deinit.
Return failed PDEV attachment through dp_context_free_mem, matching normal
teardown, and unregister its minidump record before returning it to the pool.
Context get/put retain the same pointer and zero/reuse semantics; DMA coherent,
multipage descriptor, other context and unaligned ring allocations stay on
their existing allocators. No reclaim settings, retry loop or HW addresses
are changed. Verify ordinary data, monitor observation and unloading anew.

diff --git a/qcacld-3.0/core/dp/txrx3.0/dp_txrx.c b/qcacld-3.0/core/dp/txrx3.0/dp_txrx.c
--- a/qcacld-3.0/core/dp/txrx3.0/dp_txrx.c
+++ b/qcacld-3.0/core/dp/txrx3.0/dp_txrx.c
@@ -622,7 +622,10 @@
 			dp_warn("i %d: context in use while free", i);
 
 		if (cp->addr) {
-			qdf_mem_free(cp->addr);
+			if (cp->ctxt_type == DP_PDEV_TYPE)
+				qdf_mem_vfree(cp->addr);
+			else
+				qdf_mem_free(cp->addr);
 			cp->addr = NULL;
 		}
 	}
@@ -743,7 +746,13 @@
 	/*Context pre-alloc*/
 	for (i = 0; i < QDF_ARRAY_SIZE(g_dp_context_allocs); i++) {
 		cp = &g_dp_context_allocs[i];
-		cp->addr = qdf_mem_malloc(cp->size);
+		/* The PDEV object is host-only context, not a DMA ring or
+		 * descriptor. Avoid its observed order-5 allocation failure
+		 * after normal phone use fragments physical memory. */
+		if (cp->ctxt_type == DP_PDEV_TYPE)
+			cp->addr = qdf_mem_valloc(cp->size);
+		else
+			cp->addr = qdf_mem_malloc(cp->size);
 
 		if (qdf_unlikely(!cp->addr) && cp->is_critical) {
 			dp_warn("i %d: unable to preallocate %d bytes memory!",
diff --git a/qca-wifi-host-cmn/dp/wifi3.0/dp_main.c b/qca-wifi-host-cmn/dp/wifi3.0/dp_main.c
--- a/qca-wifi-host-cmn/dp/wifi3.0/dp_main.c
+++ b/qca-wifi-host-cmn/dp/wifi3.0/dp_main.c
@@ -5800,7 +5800,10 @@
 	wlan_cfg_pdev_detach(pdev->wlan_cfg_ctx);
 fail1:
 	soc->pdev_list[pdev_id] = NULL;
-	qdf_mem_free(pdev);
+	wlan_minidump_remove(pdev, sizeof(*pdev), soc->ctrl_psoc,
+			     WLAN_MD_DP_PDEV, "dp_pdev");
+	/* Match the allocating context pool and normal detach path. */
+	dp_context_free_mem(soc, DP_PDEV_TYPE, pdev);
 fail0:
 	return QDF_STATUS_E_FAILURE;
 }
